#N canvas 20 20 3300 2400 12;
#X text 20 20 m_volca -- the Korg Volca FM's device layer \, and the only file that talks to it. Output-only: the Volca transmits nothing \, so nothing is decoded and nothing goes on param. ref/device/volca.md, f 84;
#X text 20 150 creation arg 1: the Pd channel the Volca's own channel 1 lands on (49 on the device) \, required. inlet 1: selector-prefixed -- notes <note> <vel> <dur> \, cc <controller> <value> \, program <n> \, note <note> <vel>. outlets: none., f 84;
#X text 20 250 Wired from u_map \, not sent: no bus carries a sounding note (C-2). Selector-prefixed \, so a new capability costs one route argument here and nothing in u_map or u_root (ref/architecture.md)., f 84;
#X obj 20 460 inlet;
#X obj 20 540 route notes cc program note;
#X obj 20 660 unpack f f f;
#X obj 20 800 makenote;
#X obj 20 1000 noteout;
#X obj 460 660 unpack f f;
#X obj 460 740 t b f;
#X obj 460 830 f;
#X obj 460 1000 ctlout;
#X obj 900 660 + 1;
#X obj 900 1000 pgmout;
#X obj 1300 660 t b;
#X msg 1300 730 fail m_volca bad-selector;
#X obj 1300 800 s err;
#X obj 1780 900 loadbang;
#X obj 1780 950 f \$1;
#X obj 1780 1000 t f f f f;
#X text 1780 1060 The channel goes in cold \, off the right outlets \, before any value can arrive \, and not as a creation argument: Pd 0.49 does not warn about an extra one (item 63)., f 60;
#X text 20 1080 unpack fires right to left \, so duration and velocity are in makenote before the note triggers it. makenote owns the note-offs \, so a dropped cord or a reload cannot leave the Volca droning., f 60;
#X text 460 1100 The t b f is load-bearing: ctlout's controller is its cold inlet and unpack sends the value first \, so wired straight through every CC would go to the previous controller., f 56;
#X text 900 1080 + 1 because pgmout is 1-based (item 228): this inlet means the wire number Korg and Pajen use., f 60;
#X text 1300 870 The reject is a real error \, the opposite of u_map's: the Volca transmits nothing \, so this is the only way to learn that u_map and this file disagree. C-8, f 66;
#X text 20 1300 WHAT IS NOT HERE: aftertouch and pitch bend \, which the Volca ignores in any firmware \; and any notion of what a note MEANS -- this file is told what to play and plays it. ⛔ CLOCK AND TRANSPORT ARE NOT HERE EITHER \, AND THEY DO NOT REACH THIS DEVICE AT ALL. An earlier version of this comment said they were u_tempo's and "already reach every port". They reach ONE: u_tempo's realtime-out holds one midiout for them \, set at loadbang to port 1 -- the Launchpad. Port 3 \, the SP-404's \, had them too until the 404 left the rig on 2026-11-04. The Volca is port 4 and the nano is port 2 \, so neither has ever had a clock byte from this instrument. Measured with aseqdump on the hardware 2026-08-10 \, item 279: five seconds on Pd's Midi-Out 4 produced nothing at all. ⚠️ THAT MEANS THE VOLCA CANNOT SYNC \, which is a gap rather than a decision -- see plan-v04.md., f 84;
#X text 900 1300 Velocity and program change need the Pajen 1.09 firmware and two of its global settings (Reference \, korg-volca-fm \, Pajen 1.09 firmware)., f 60;
#X text 1300 380 route leaves a remainder starting with a float \, which is a list \, so unpack takes it with no list append. program leaves the lone float that + 1 wants., f 76;
#X obj 20 1700 loadbang;
#X obj 20 1750 del 2000;
#X obj 20 1800 f \$1;
#X obj 20 1850 print m_volca-channel;
#X text 300 1750 Prints the channel it got: the Volca transmits nothing \, so a wrong channel is otherwise invisible. C-9, f 66;
#X obj 1400 1440 loadbang;
#X msg 1400 1500 expect m_volca none;
#X obj 1400 1560 s presence;
#X text 1750 1440 none is a kind: the Volca transmits nothing \, so it registers as undetectable on purpose rather than being left out by mistake. u_present's whole-rig re-wire still brings it back (ref/module/presence.md)., f 44;
#X obj 2300 660 unpack f f;
#X obj 2500 1900 r panic;
#X obj 2500 1960 t b;
#X msg 2500 2020 0;
#X obj 2500 2080 ctlout 123;
#X text 2300 740 note bypasses makenote \, because a held key must not release itself: the off comes from the key \, as velocity 0 from u_map's volca-key. The panic path covers the droning makenote prevents. It reuses the one noteout \, so MIDI_EXPECT stays noteout:2., f 62;
#X text 2700 1900 Panic is All Notes Off \, CC 123 \, since the note inlet can leave a note sounding. The value is 0 and the controller the creation argument \, so only the channel has to arrive., f 62;
